@page "/components/navigation-menu"

<PageTitle>Navigation Menu — Unpoly.Blazor.Shadcn</PageTitle>

<h1 class="doc-h1">Navigation Menu</h1>
<p class="doc-lede">
    A <code>&lt;nav&gt;</code> around a real <code>&lt;ul&gt;</code>, so the landmark and the item count are announced. Each panel is its own popover in the top layer rather than a slot in one shared viewport.
</p>

<p class="doc-note">
    A <code>&lt;nav&gt;</code> around a real <code>&lt;ul&gt;</code>. Radix animates every panel
    through one shared viewport so they cross-fade; each panel here is its own popover in the top
    layer instead — no cross-fade, and in exchange nothing clips it and there is no z-index to
    lose. Put <code>[up-nav]</code> on it and Unpoly marks the current link.
</p>
<Example Source="NavigationMenuExample.razor"><NavigationMenuExample /></Example>

<h2 class="doc-h2">Link Component</h2>
<p class="doc-note">
    shadcn writes <code>asChild</code> here so the link can be a router <code>Link</code>. There is
    no router: it is an <code>&lt;a href&gt;</code>, and <code>[up-nav]</code> on the list marks the
    current one — Unpoly compares each href with the address bar, which keeps working after a
    fragment swap because the swap is what changed the address bar.
</p>
